Min Flips for Alternate
Difficulty: EasyAccuracy: 48.58%Submissions: 64K+Points: 2
Given a binary string s, we can flip any bit (change 0 to 1 or 1 to 0) to make the string alternating. A string is called alternating if no two adjacent characters are the same.

Find the minimum number of bit flips required to make t








class Solution {
  public:
    int minFlips(string &s) {
        int n=s.size(),ct=0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++) if(s[i]-'0'!=(i%2)) ct++;
        return min(ct,n-ct);
    }
};


